# AI Agent Prism - Environment Variables Configuration Template
# 
# INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Copy this file to .env in the root directory
# 2. Fill in your actual values (DO NOT commit .env to version control)
# 3. For Cloud Run deployment, set these as environment variables in the service configuration
#
# Copy command:
#   cp env.example .env
#   # Then edit .env with your actual values

# ============================================
# REQUIRED - Core GCP Configuration
# ============================================

# Your Google Cloud Project ID (deploy_all.sh overwrites this from versions.env)
# Primary project for this repo: agentic-prismv333 (do not use other GCP projects for deploys here).
# Find in: Cloud Console > IAM & Admin > Settings > Project ID
GCP_PROJECT_ID=agentic-prismv333

# Your Google Cloud Project Number (numeric)
# agentic-prismv333 → run: gcloud projects describe agentic-prismv333 --format="value(projectNumber)"
GCP_PROJECT_NUMBER=766986452720

# GCP Region/Location for Vertex AI services
# Default: us-west1
# Options: us-central1, us-east1, europe-west1, asia-east1, etc.
GCP_LOCATION=us-west1

# Model Version (default: gemini-3.0-pro)
MODEL_VERSION=gemini-2.5-pro

# ============================================
# REQUIRED - Vertex AI Search (Discovery Engine)
# ============================================

# Data Store ID for Events knowledge base
# This is created when you run: python backend/setup_kb.py
# Example: "event-web-knowledge_gcs_store" or "events-web-knowledge"
# Find in: Cloud Console > Vertex AI Search > Data Stores
VERTEX_SEARCH_DATA_STORE_ID=event-web-knowledge_gcs_store

# ============================================
# OPTIONAL - Enterprise Edition Only
# ============================================

# Engine ID for Vertex AI Search Enterprise Edition
# Only required if using Enterprise Edition with Engine-based search
# Leave empty or omit if using Standard Edition (Data Store only)
# Example: "event-agent_1769803344912"
# Find in: Cloud Console > Vertex AI Search > Engines
VERTEX_SEARCH_ENGINE_ID=event-agent_1769803344912

# ============================================
# OPTIONAL - IAP smoke tests (scripts/smoke_glass_ui_departments.py)
# ============================================
# If Cloud Run is behind Identity-Aware Proxy, gcloud auth print-identity-token --audiences=...
# only works for service accounts. For a user account, use Python fetch_id_token with the IAP
# OAuth 2.0 client ID from: Console → Security → Identity-Aware Proxy → your HTTPS resource.
# IAP_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=123456789-xxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GLASS_UI_URL=https://YOUR-SERVICE-....run.app   # gcloud run services describe ... --format='value(status.url)'

# ============================================
# OPTIONAL - Agent Engine (correct flow: UI → Supervisor → department agents)
# ============================================
#
# Full resource name of the Supervisor Agent Engine. When set, the UI sends
# messages to the Supervisor in Vertex AI; Supervisor invokes eng_lead /
# xray_manager / events / chat inside the engine (agent identities, no backend Gemini).
# Get from repo root: python scripts/get_agent_engine_id.py supervisor
# Example: projects/YOUR_PROJECT_ID/locations/us-west1/reasoningEngines/<id>
# AGENTIC_LENS_SUPERVISOR_ENGINE=

# Agent Engine stream timeouts (seconds). One UI request calls Supervisor then a department engine in series.
# Department default in code is 600s (Engineering). Keep Cloud Run /api/query timeout above their sum.
# AGENT_ENGINE_SUPERVISOR_TIMEOUT_S=300
# AGENT_ENGINE_DEPARTMENT_TIMEOUT_S=1200
#
# If the UI shows HTTP 504 with body "upstream request timeout", a load balancer or IAP in front of Cloud Run
# is likely timing out before the app (defaults are often 30–60s). Raise that backend/proxy timeout to match
# Cloud Run (deploy-glass-ui.sh sets GLASS_UI_CLOUD_RUN_TIMEOUT_S, default 1800).
#
# Department engine resource names (full projects/.../reasoningEngines/...). Pass to Cloud Run via deploy-glass-ui.sh:
# CHAT_ENGINE_ID=...
# ENG_ENGINE_ID=...
# EVENTS_ENGINE_ID=...
# XRAY_ENGINE_ID=...
#
# Engineering squad (eng_lead calls these engines directly). Set in Agent Engine env for eng_lead, or locally in .env:
# AGENTIC_LENS_ENGINE_SCOUT=projects/.../locations/.../reasoningEngines/...
# AGENTIC_LENS_ENGINE_CODER=projects/.../locations/.../reasoningEngines/...
# AGENTIC_LENS_ENGINE_QUALITY_AND_SECURITY_REVIEWER=projects/.../locations/.../reasoningEngines/...

# ============================================
# OPTIONAL - Infra (VPC-SC step 12)
# ============================================
# When running ./infra/apply.sh, step 12 (VPC-SC) allows only these identities to ingress/egress the perimeter.
# Set one of (or export before running apply):
#   VPC_SC_ALLOWED_USER_EMAIL=you@example.com
#   VPC_SC_ALLOWED_MEMBERS=user:a@b.com,serviceAccount:svc@project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# If unset, uses current gcloud account (gcloud config get-value account).

# ============================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================
#
# 1. Get your Project ID and Project Number:
#    - Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com/iam-admin/settings
#    - Or: gcloud projects list
#    - Or: gcloud projects describe YOUR_PROJECT_ID
#
# 2. Create the Data Store (if not already created):
#    python backend/setup_kb.py
#    This will output your DATA_STORE_ID
#
# 3. For Enterprise Edition, get your Engine ID:
#    - Cloud Console > Vertex AI Search > Engines
#    - Or check the setup output
#
# 4. Copy this file to .env and fill in values:
#    cp env.example .env
#    # Edit .env with your actual values
#
# 5. For Cloud Run deployment, set these as environment variables:
#    gcloud run services update SERVICE_NAME \
#        --set-env-vars GCP_PROJECT_ID=xxx,GCP_PROJECT_NUMBER=xxx,...
#
